# The peer-offline case (docs/pageflip.md section 4), LEFT half: it stays running while the other
# instance quits under it, which is what a device powering off or walking out of range looks like
# from here -- no farewell, just silence.
#
# The point is not the notice. It is that presence stops licensing the two-step advance: a device
# still advancing by two with nothing on the other end is a reader that silently skips every other
# page. So the press below must land ONE page on.
#
# Deliberately `wait` rather than `expect peer went quiet`. ScriptDriver matches expects against a
# 256-line ring, and that notice is followed inside the same frame by hundreds of image-render debug
# lines -- it is evicted before the next tick can see it. The harness greps the whole log for it
# instead, which no amount of logging can drown.
log pageflip-offline-left: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
wait 9000
expect peer present
wait 2000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-off-left-00.bmp
# The right half leaves at about eleven seconds in; presence expires four missed heartbeats later.
wait 22000
tap down
wait 5000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-off-left-01.bmp
wait 1000
log pageflip-offline-left: done
quit
